# Orrery

*(Thanks to Berkan)*

A clockwork solar system with no mutable state at all. There is no `update`
anywhere. Each frame, Target replaces the assemblage with `tick()`, a new
System identical to the old one except that its clock reads one more. A
planet's position is a pure function of `time.t`, and so is each moon's.
Nothing walks the planets, nothing stores an angle, and nothing can drift out
of sync, because there is exactly one number in the whole assemblage that
changes.

The Schema reads as a description of the thing:

- a System is a Sun, some Planets, and a clock
- a Planet is a name, an orbit, a period, a size, a colour, a starting phase, and some Moons
- a Moon is an orbit, a period, a size, and a starting phase

Drawing is hierarchical without any mutation: the System hands the pen and the
sun's centre to each planet with a `fold`, and each planet hands the pen and
its own centre to its moons. Moons orbit planets because that is what the
drawing says, not because any code copies coordinates.

## Schema

```
System = Sun [Planet]/planets Time
Sun = Float/x Float/y Float/size
Planet = String/name Float/orbit Float/period Float/size Int/colour Float/phase [Moon]/moons
Moon = Float/orbit Float/period Float/size Float/phase
Time = Int/t
```

## Construction

```
[:System
  [:Sun 400.0 300.0 22.0]
  [:Array/Planet
    [:Planet "Mercury"  48.0   88.0  3.0 11184810 0.0 [:Array/Moon]]
    [:Planet "Venus"    78.0  225.0  5.5 15453289 1.2 [:Array/Moon]]
    [:Planet "Earth"   112.0  365.0  6.0  4359642 2.8 [:Array/Moon [:Moon 13.0 27.0 1.8 0.0]]]
    [:Planet "Mars"    150.0  687.0  4.0 13527844 4.1 [:Array/Moon [:Moon 8.0 8.0 1.0 0.0] [:Moon 11.0 30.0 1.0 2.0]]]
    [:Planet "Jupiter" 215.0 1200.0 13.0 14000730 0.7
      [:Array/Moon [:Moon 19.0 18.0 1.5 0.0] [:Moon 23.0 36.0 1.6 1.0] [:Moon 28.0 72.0 2.0 2.0] [:Moon 35.0 170.0 1.8 3.0]]]
    [:Planet "Saturn"  275.0 2900.0 11.0 15258743 5.5 [:Array/Moon [:Moon 22.0 160.0 2.0 0.0]]]
  ]
  [:Time 0]
]
```

## Methods

```
System::tick = { [:System sun planets [:Time (time.t + 1)]] }

Moon::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g, Float/cx, Float/cy, Int/t, @WCHNTMaths/m |
  a = phase + (t * (0.9 / period)).
  g.beginFill(13421772).drawCircle(cx + (m.cos(a) * orbit), cy + (m.sin(a) * orbit), size).endFill()
}

Planet::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g, Sun/sun, Int/t, @WCHNTMaths/m |
  a = phase + (t * (0.35 / period)).
  px = sun.x + (m.cos(a) * orbit).
  py = sun.y + (m.sin(a) * orbit).
  ring = g.lineStyle(1, 2236962).drawCircle(sun.x, sun.y, orbit).noStroke().
  body = g.beginFill(colour).drawCircle(px, py, size).endFill().
  moons.fold(g, { acc, Moon/mo | drawn = mo.draw(acc, px, py, t, m). acc })
}

System::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g, @WCHNTMaths/m |
  lit = g.beginFill(16768640).drawCircle(sun.x, sun.y, sun.size).endFill().
  planets.fold(g, { acc, Planet/p | drawn = p.draw(acc, sun, time.t, m). acc })
}
```


## Target

```
%canvas

%requires
WCHNTMaths::sin(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::cos(Float) -> Float

%init
var system;

function init() {
    system = SystemAssemblage.factory();
    wchntGraphics.background(0x05070d, 0.5);
}

%step
function step() {
    system = system.tick();
    wchntGraphics.clear();
    system.draw(wchntGraphics, wchntMaths);
}
```
